WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.640 --> 00:00:04.880
Netflix is a genuine treasure trove&nbsp;
when it comes to movies — and many&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.880 --> 00:00:09.520
of the platform's original productions are&nbsp;
counted among the most exciting releases of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:09.520 --> 00:00:15.040
the last few years. Here's a look at the&nbsp;
10 most-watched Netflix original movies,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:15.040 --> 00:00:18.240
ranked according to their&nbsp;
ratings on Rotten Tomatoes.

00:00:19.120 --> 00:00:25.600
In 2019, a stunning 83 million viewers tuned&nbsp;
in to watch Michael Bay's streaming debut;&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:25.600 --> 00:00:31.680
6 Underground. The film's Rotten Tomatoes&nbsp;
stands at 36%, but critics weren't really the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:31.680 --> 00:00:36.240
intended audience to begin with. And the score&nbsp;
actually places it squarely in the middle of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:36.240 --> 00:00:41.760
Bay's filmography, review-wise. So if you're a&nbsp;
fan of the director's trademark frenetic action&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:41.760 --> 00:00:46.400
stylings, this will be right up your&nbsp;
alley. It's a crowd pleaser, to be sure.

00:00:46.400 --> 00:00:50.720
The plot centers on an elite group of&nbsp;
mercenaries who have faked their own deaths&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:50.720 --> 00:00:55.920
in order to carry out missions off the grid.&nbsp;
Their assignment: travel to the fictional land&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:55.920 --> 00:01:00.960
of Turgistan to replace the country's&nbsp;
brutal dictator with his imprisoned brother.

00:01:00.960 --> 00:01:04.400
With its loud explosions,&nbsp;
snappy action-movie dialogue,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:04.400 --> 00:01:10.400
and an unrelenting pace, 6 Underground is without&nbsp;
a doubt a prime cut Michael Bay production — and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:10.400 --> 00:01:14.800
if that sounds like your kind of thing, then&nbsp;
you're bound to find it a whole heap of fun.

00:01:15.840 --> 00:01:20.480
Hollywood power partners Mark Wahlberg and&nbsp;
director Peter Berg have produced a number&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:20.480 --> 00:01:26.480
of great movies — including Lone Survivor,&nbsp;
Deepwater Horizon, and Patriots Day. Sadly,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:26.480 --> 00:01:31.040
Spenser Confidential didn't quite earn&nbsp;
the same rave reviews as those pictures.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:31.040 --> 00:01:37.840
A 37% Rotten Tomatoes score didn't stop 85 million&nbsp;
people from streaming this throwback cop movie,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:37.840 --> 00:01:40.640
making it one of the platform's biggest ever hits.

00:01:40.640 --> 00:01:45.760
The movie is an adaptation of Robert B.&nbsp;
Parker's popular Spenser novels, with Wahlberg&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:45.760 --> 00:01:50.480
stepping into the famous detective's shoes.&nbsp;
Spenser is a cop who plays by his own rules,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:50.480 --> 00:01:55.120
which doesn't play so well at a time when&nbsp;
police brutality is under heightened scrutiny.

00:01:55.120 --> 00:02:00.000
The script is co-written by Oscar-winner Brian&nbsp;
Helgeland, and it gives Wahlberg plenty of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:05.360
excuses to kick ass with his partner and cut&nbsp;
it up with his wise-cracking buddy. Meanwhile,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:05.360 --> 00:02:10.560
a number of amusing cameos by famous faces&nbsp;
help liven things up between all the action.

00:02:10.560 --> 00:02:13.760
Since it's based on just one&nbsp;
book in the Spenser series,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:13.760 --> 00:02:17.440
and considering the huge number of people&nbsp;
who watched it, it's hard to imagine&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:17.440 --> 00:02:22.240
Wahlberg won't holster up for a sequel&nbsp;
as the famous detective sometime soon.

00:02:23.200 --> 00:02:29.200
In 2014, Adam Sandler's Happy Madison Productions&nbsp;
signed a lucrative deal with Netflix that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:29.200 --> 00:02:34.160
has since produced some of the comedian's most&nbsp;
widely viewed films. The most-watched among them,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:34.160 --> 00:02:38.560
Murder Mystery, brought in 83 million&nbsp;
viewers, which in box office terms would&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:38.560 --> 00:02:43.680
make it a financial success on par with The&nbsp;
Waterboy. It also earned pretty good reviews,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:43.680 --> 00:02:49.120
relative to most Sandler comedies,&nbsp;
earning a 44% score on Rotten Tomatoes.

00:02:49.120 --> 00:02:53.600
The film reunites Sandler with his Just&nbsp;
Go With It co-star Jennifer Aniston,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:53.600 --> 00:02:58.480
and it allows the Sandman to vacation in&nbsp;
exotic locales with his best buds for the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:58.480 --> 00:03:03.440
cause of comedy. The movie's script is sharp&nbsp;
and sprightly enough to keep everyone else as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:03.440 --> 00:03:05.440
entertained as the people who made it.

00:03:05.440 --> 00:03:09.200
The premise: Sandler and Aniston are a&nbsp;
couple traveling through Europe on their&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:09.200 --> 00:03:13.520
15th wedding anniversary. On the plane,&nbsp;
they meet a mysterious billionaire who&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:13.520 --> 00:03:18.160
invites them to party on his yacht with&nbsp;
his elderly uncle. While at sea, however,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:18.160 --> 00:03:23.680
the uncle is found killed with his own dagger —&nbsp;
and Sandler and Aniston are the main suspects.

00:03:23.680 --> 00:03:24.640
"Audrey."

00:03:24.640 --> 00:03:25.140
"Yep."

00:03:25.520 --> 00:03:26.800
"Get the cocktail sauce."

00:03:26.800 --> 00:03:30.400
Released the same year as Sandler's&nbsp;
critically acclaimed Uncut Gems,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:30.400 --> 00:03:35.920
Murder Mystery finds the actor in the familiarly&nbsp;
goofy territory lots of fans want to see&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:35.920 --> 00:03:41.360
from the funnyman. For that reason alone, it's&nbsp;
perhaps no mystery why so many people tuned in.

00:03:42.320 --> 00:03:46.160
George Clooney's sci-fi epic&nbsp;
The Midnight Sky earned a 50%&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:46.160 --> 00:03:50.800
Rotten Tomatoes score. Critics noticed that the&nbsp;
movie has more than a few things going for it,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:50.800 --> 00:03:55.760
bringing in 72 million viewers and earning&nbsp;
an Oscar nomination for its visual effects.

00:03:55.760 --> 00:04:00.320
Clooney stars as Augustine, a dying&nbsp;
scientist stranded on an Earth that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:00.320 --> 00:04:05.360
has been ravaged by an unseen disaster. Left&nbsp;
alone at a research facility in the Arctic,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:05.360 --> 00:04:09.920
he attempts to warn off any spaceships on&nbsp;
their way back to the desolated planet.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:09.920 --> 00:04:15.680
When he finds himself unable to reach the incoming&nbsp;
crew of the "Aether," Augustine travels across the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:15.680 --> 00:04:20.320
frozen tundra to warn them — but the ship's&nbsp;
crew are having a few problems of their own.

00:04:20.320 --> 00:04:25.840
The two halves of The Midnight Sky really come&nbsp;
together in a third-act twist that links an&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:25.840 --> 00:04:29.040
emotional through-line between&nbsp;
them. Along with the story,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:29.040 --> 00:04:32.480
the technical aspects of the&nbsp;
film are unarguably stunning,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:32.480 --> 00:04:37.040
from Martin Ruhe's cinematography to&nbsp;
Alexandre Desplat's heartbreaking score.

00:04:38.000 --> 00:04:41.920
As the summer of 2020 dragged on, it&nbsp;
became increasingly clear that the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:41.920 --> 00:04:46.160
pandemic would keep theaters closed.&nbsp;
So naturally audiences increasingly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:46.160 --> 00:04:50.720
turned to streaming services to get their&nbsp;
blockbuster kicks. It's little wonder, then,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:50.720 --> 00:04:56.400
that 75 million people watched the high-concept&nbsp;
action thriller Project Power when it dropped&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:56.400 --> 00:05:01.600
on Netflix that August. The movie also&nbsp;
netted a 61% Rotten Tomatoes rating.

00:05:01.600 --> 00:05:04.800
In an era dominated by&nbsp;
mainstream comic book movies,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:04.800 --> 00:05:10.560
Project Power imagines a stranger scenario —&nbsp;
one in which anyone can become a superhero by&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:10.560 --> 00:05:15.280
taking an experimental drug. The catch:&nbsp;
the effects only last for five minutes,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:15.280 --> 00:05:20.960
and there's no telling what superpower you might&nbsp;
gain… or whether you'll use it for good or evil.

00:05:20.960 --> 00:05:25.040
Chaos predictably ensues when the&nbsp;
drug hits the streets of New Orleans,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:25.040 --> 00:05:29.440
so teenager Robin teams up with a local&nbsp;
cop and an ex-soldier to track down the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:29.440 --> 00:05:33.200
evil pharmaceutical company who made&nbsp;
it. As the critics will tell you,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:33.200 --> 00:05:37.600
the true power of this film comes from its&nbsp;
impressive performances and thrilling action&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:37.600 --> 00:05:42.240
sequences. And there's still plenty of room to&nbsp;
add more to the intriguing story in a sequel.

00:05:43.040 --> 00:05:47.280
It seems like only yesterday that the Bird&nbsp;
Box challenge was sweeping the nation,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:47.280 --> 00:05:52.320
forcing Netflix to issue a public plea for&nbsp;
people to stop walking around while blindfolded.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:52.320 --> 00:05:57.040
Released during the holiday season of&nbsp;
2018, this movie does for sight what&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:57.040 --> 00:06:02.080
A Quiet Place did for sound. And just like&nbsp;
that horror hit, Bird Box was a sensation,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:02.080 --> 00:06:07.040
bringing in a total of 89 million&nbsp;
viewers and a 63% Rotten Tomatoes score.

00:06:07.040 --> 00:06:11.680
Adapted from the novel by Josh Malerman,&nbsp;
the movie stars Sandra Bullock as Malorie,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:11.680 --> 00:06:16.320
an expectant mother whose fears of becoming&nbsp;
a parent are quickly set aside for an even&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:16.320 --> 00:06:20.560
greater terror. To reveal much more would&nbsp;
spoil the movie's fascinating premise,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:20.560 --> 00:06:24.480
but it's probably fair to say that the scene in&nbsp;
which Malorie and her children make their way&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:24.480 --> 00:06:29.280
through the woods is among the most iconic&nbsp;
horror sequences of the last few years.

00:06:29.280 --> 00:06:32.720
Susanne Bier creates a constant&nbsp;
sense of dread and tension&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:32.720 --> 00:06:37.120
throughout Bird Box, relying on good&nbsp;
old-fashioned suspense and atmosphere&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:37.120 --> 00:06:41.440
over flashy special effects. She also&nbsp;
does a good job with her ensemble,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:41.440 --> 00:06:45.920
eliciting performances that keep you invested&nbsp;
in the human story at the heart of it all.

00:06:46.720 --> 00:06:52.480
With 99 million viewers, Extraction is the&nbsp;
most-watched film in Netflix's history,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:52.480 --> 00:06:57.760
and there's certainly a good reason for that:&nbsp;
the film hit the streaming site in April 2020,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:57.760 --> 00:07:02.720
just as the coronavirus pandemic was forcing the&nbsp;
closure of movie theaters across the country.

00:07:02.720 --> 00:07:06.480
The movie earned a 67% approval&nbsp;
rating on Rotten Tomatoes,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:06.480 --> 00:07:12.160
and the high viewership was more than enough to&nbsp;
justify a sequel — and perhaps even a franchise.

00:07:12.160 --> 00:07:17.680
Directed by Sam Hargrave from a script by Joe&nbsp;
Russo, Extraction has got all the trappings of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:17.680 --> 00:07:23.360
a whiz-bang action blockbuster. Chris Hemsworth&nbsp;
stars as Tyler Rake, a mercenary tasked with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:23.360 --> 00:07:28.800
rescuing the son of an imprisoned Indian crime&nbsp;
lord who's been kidnapped by his father's rivals.

00:07:28.800 --> 00:07:33.920
Extraction's action is its best quality,&nbsp;
being masterfully directed by Hargrave,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:33.920 --> 00:07:37.760
who had previously worked as a stunt&nbsp;
coordinator on Hemsworth's various&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:37.760 --> 00:07:42.720
Marvel Cinematic Universe films. He also&nbsp;
makes the most out of the film's R rating,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:42.720 --> 00:07:48.160
spilling blood by the bucketful and bringing a&nbsp;
real intensity to the film's action sequences.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:48.160 --> 00:07:51.360
What more could you want from&nbsp;
a punchy lockdown blockbuster?

00:07:52.480 --> 00:07:58.720
Zack Snyder dominated the streaming services&nbsp;
in early 2021. Shortly after his four-hour&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:58.720 --> 00:08:04.240
director's cut of Justice League hit HBO Max,&nbsp;
the director released the grisly horror flick&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:04.240 --> 00:08:09.760
Army of the Dead on Netflix. It didn't take long&nbsp;
for Army of the Dead to crack the streamer's Top&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:09.760 --> 00:08:16.720
10 most viewed films, racking in a staggering&nbsp;
72 million viewers. Plus, the movie's 68%&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:16.720 --> 00:08:22.240
Rotten Tomatoes score places it in the top half of&nbsp;
Snyder's filmography from a critical standpoint.

00:08:22.240 --> 00:08:26.880
Considering Snyder's first film was a remake&nbsp;
of George A. Romero's Dawn of the Dead,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:26.880 --> 00:08:32.640
it's only fitting that he would one day return to&nbsp;
the zombie genre. Army of the Dead is a sly hybrid&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:32.640 --> 00:08:38.800
of horror and heist movies, following a mercenary&nbsp;
who is tasked with recovering $200 million from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:38.800 --> 00:08:44.560
a casino vault in a zombie-infested Las Vegas,&nbsp;
before the military nukes the city off the map.

00:08:44.560 --> 00:08:47.600
Snyder seems to paint the&nbsp;
screen with blood in this movie,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:47.600 --> 00:08:52.560
making the most of his hard-R rating. The&nbsp;
supporting cast helps liven things up, too,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:52.560 --> 00:08:58.480
most notably Tig Notaro as one of lead&nbsp;
actor Dave Bautista's gang of thieves.

00:08:58.480 --> 00:09:00.080
"Hundred percent, I'm in."

00:09:00.800 --> 00:09:03.040
"You don't want to know the risks, or…"

00:09:03.040 --> 00:09:04.560
"Why would I want to know the risks?"

00:09:04.560 --> 00:09:06.400
For fans of Snyder and his flashy,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:06.400 --> 00:09:10.080
stylized type of movie, it really&nbsp;
doesn't get much better than this.

00:09:11.120 --> 00:09:15.040
One of the surprise hits of the&nbsp;
pandemic summer was The Old Guard,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:15.040 --> 00:09:20.720
which hit Netflix in July 2020. All&nbsp;
in all, 78 million viewers tuned in,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:20.720 --> 00:09:26.400
with interest undoubtedly piqued by the&nbsp;
movie's sterling 80% score on Rotten Tomatoes.

00:09:26.400 --> 00:09:31.600
Charlize Theron stars as Andy, the immortal&nbsp;
leader of an elite squad of mercenaries.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:31.600 --> 00:09:36.320
Together with her brothers-in-arms, Andy&nbsp;
travels the globe protecting mortals — and,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:36.320 --> 00:09:41.040
along the way, picks up a soldier who&nbsp;
discovers that she too is unable to die.

00:09:41.040 --> 00:09:46.240
In adapting writer Greg Rucka and artist&nbsp;
Leandro Fernandez's graphic novel,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:46.240 --> 00:09:51.920
director Gina Prince-Bythewood infuses the&nbsp;
superhero genre with the sublime passions&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:51.920 --> 00:09:57.200
of her previous films. What's really special about&nbsp;
The Old Guard is the way in which Prince-Bythewood&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:57.200 --> 00:10:02.000
so deftly balances the movie's more&nbsp;
emotional scenes with its action sequences.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:02.000 --> 00:10:06.320
Those elements work in perfect harmony&nbsp;
with Theron, who brings plenty of emotional&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:06.320 --> 00:10:12.000
heft to her performance — and once again&nbsp;
proves herself to be an apt action star.

00:10:12.000 --> 00:10:16.960
At a time when Marvel and DC have taken&nbsp;
great pains to create interconnected sagas&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:16.960 --> 00:10:21.520
geared towards mass consumption, The Old&nbsp;
Guard is proof that an original vision&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:21.520 --> 00:10:24.560
can break through — and find&nbsp;
a mass audience to boot.

00:10:25.360 --> 00:10:30.880
The Netflix smash hit Enola Holmes raked&nbsp;
in 76 million viewers during the fall&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:30.880 --> 00:10:35.280
of 2020. It's also one of the platform's&nbsp;
most critically acclaimed titles,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:35.280 --> 00:10:38.960
with a certified fresh 91% Rotten Tomatoes rating.

00:10:38.960 --> 00:10:43.680
Millie Bobby Brown plays Enola Holmes, a&nbsp;
teenage sleuth who's following in the footsteps&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:43.680 --> 00:10:48.640
of her famous older sibling, Sherlock. While&nbsp;
Sherlock is happy to encourage her sleuthing,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:48.640 --> 00:10:54.000
her other brother, Mycroft, thinks she'd be better&nbsp;
placed learning etiquette at finishing school.

00:10:54.000 --> 00:10:55.600
"I don't want a husband!"

00:10:55.600 --> 00:10:58.560
"And that is another thing you&nbsp;
need to have educated out of you."

00:10:58.560 --> 00:11:02.160
When her mother goes missing, however,&nbsp;
it's up to Enola to track her down,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:02.160 --> 00:11:06.160
deciphering clues from a variety of&nbsp;
birthday presents she left behind.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:06.160 --> 00:11:11.200
Her investigation uncovers a vast conspiracy&nbsp;
revolving around a young aristocrat,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:11.200 --> 00:11:16.000
who's similarly trying to break free of&nbsp;
the societal restraints placed upon him.

00:11:16.000 --> 00:11:21.600
It's not difficult to see why this was such a hit.&nbsp;
Enola Holmes is just dangerous and droll enough to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:21.600 --> 00:11:26.880
have some real edge, while providing teenage&nbsp;
viewers with an uplifting girl-power message.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:26.880 --> 00:11:31.680
Considering it's based on just one book from&nbsp;
Nancy Springer's popular Young Adult series,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:31.680 --> 00:11:36.080
it's also safe to say the adventures&nbsp;
of Enola Holmes are far from finished.

00:11:36.880 --> 00:11:39.680
Check out one of our newest&nbsp;
videos right here! Plus,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:39.680 --> 00:11:43.520
even more Looper videos about your&nbsp;
favorite movies are coming soon.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:43.520 --> 00:11:49.814
Subscribe to our YouTube channel and hit&nbsp;
the bell so you don't miss a single one.

